WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Hang a load from a spring weighing scale.

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:06.660
The spring stretches, and a
pointer slides down the scale.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:11.630
Now look at the markings:
1 newton, 2, 3, 4.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.190
Every gap is exactly the same.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.760
A ruler is marked out by design.

6
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.210
This is just a coil of wire.

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.960
So why are the markings on a
spring scale evenly spaced?

8
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.240
Why not bunched up at one end?

9
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:29.530
In this mission, you'll find how a
spring's force depends on its stretch,

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.110
and what makes one spring stiffer.

11
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.560
Then you'll plot a force
graph for a spring,

12
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.060
and read its stiffness from the graph.

13
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: explain why the markings
on the scale are evenly spaced.
